# Intake

Goal: get everything needed for a first draft that needs very little tweaking, in **one** well-built message,
then stop and wait for Jake.

Duda asks generic questions. We ask the questions a good designer who knows that trade would ask.

## Step 1 — Parse the prompt

From Jake's message, pull out what is stated. Write nothing else as fact.

- Business name → also make a slug (`heartwood-homes`).
- Trade(s) → map to a question-bank entry in `question-bank.md`. A business can match two
  (e.g. "general contractor/custom home builder" → GC + Custom home builder; "land clearing and stump grinding"
  → Land clearing + Tree service). If nothing fits, use the generic fallback and adapt it.
- Location (city, state).
- Anything else stated: website URL, phone, owner name, brand kit, existing photos.

Create `sites/<slug>/brief/` and start `intake.md` from `templates/intake-brief.md`. Record the prompt verbatim.

## Step 2 — Light research (before asking anything)

Do this quietly so your questions are sharper. Do not present findings as confirmed facts.

1. **Existing website.** If Jake gave a URL, go to Step 3. If not, do a quick web search for
   `"<business name>" <city>` to see if a site, Google Business Profile, Facebook page or BBB listing shows up.
   - If you find a likely match, **ask** Jake to confirm it ("Is this them: heartwoodhomes.com?"). Do not crawl
     a site Jake hasn't confirmed, and do not use anything from it yet.
   - If you find nothing, still ask (Step 4, question A).
2. **Local competitors.** Look at 3–5 competitors in the same trade and metro. Note what their sites do well and
   badly (one line each). This feeds the art directions and the "how to stand out" recommendation. Never copy
   their copy or photos.

## Step 3 — Crawl the existing site (only once confirmed)

If the client has a site and Jake confirms it (or gave it directly), crawl it. Use Playwright or fetch; stay on
that domain; respect robots.txt; max ~40 pages.

Pull, and save into `sites/<slug>/brief/assets/` + log in `sources.md`:

| Item | How | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Logo | `<header> img`, `link[rel=icon]`, `og:image`, SVG in header | Prefer SVG; else largest PNG. Note if it's low-res. |
| Photos | all `img`/`srcset`/CSS backgrounds ≥ 800px wide | Keep originals. Flag stock photos (watermarks, known stock filenames, reverse-image hits). |
| Copy | headings, service descriptions, about text | Treat as source material. We rewrite, but facts in it are citable. |
| Services | nav + service pages | List them exactly as named. |
| Reviews / testimonials | testimonial blocks, embedded Google reviews | Keep name + text + source exactly. Never edit wording. |
| Colors | computed styles of header, buttons, links; logo palette | Report hex values and where they appear. |
| Fonts | `font-family` of headings/body, Google Fonts / Typekit links | |
| Contact | phone (`tel:` links), email, address, hours | |
| Socials | links to Facebook, Instagram, Google, Houzz, Nextdoor, YouTube, LinkedIn | |
| Licensing / years / area | footer, about page, schema JSON-LD | Cite the exact page and sentence. |
| SEO | titles, meta descriptions, current URLs | Needed for redirects so we don't lose rankings. |

Every fact in `sources.md` gets: value, URL, the quoted text, date pulled. If a page says "Over 20 years of
experience", record exactly that, not "Since 2004".

Also check the Google Business Profile if findable (rating, review count, categories, hours). Mark these
"seen on <date>, must be confirmed before showing on the site", because they change.

## Step 4 — Build the question message

Rules for questions:

- Numbered, grouped, **multiple choice** with letters. Each group has a **Recommended** pick with a one-line
  reason. Always offer "Something else: ___".
- Pick questions from the question bank for the matched trade(s). Don't ask what you already know.
  Don't ask more than ~15 questions total. Prefer the ones that change the design or the page list.
- Include alternatives Jake may not have thought of (e.g. for a builder: "Show price ranges" vs "Starting at"
  vs "No pricing, explain the process instead").
- Facts you need are asked as a short fill-in list, with "unknown is fine, it stays hidden" stated clearly.

The message always contains these sections, in this order:

**A. Existing website** (always, unless Jake already said)
"Does Heartwood Homes have a website now?" a) yes: <URL?> → I'll pull logo, photos, copy, reviews and contact info,
and plan redirects; b) no; c) only a Facebook/Google profile → I'll pull what's public there.
If you found a likely match, show it here for confirmation.

**B. Brand kit** (always)
a) full kit (logo files, colors, fonts, guidelines PDF) → send it, I'll follow it exactly;
b) logo only → I'll build colors/fonts around it; c) nothing → pick an art direction below.

**C. Goals and audience** (trade-specific; from the question bank)
Main action (call / quote form / book consult / text), who the ideal customer is, job size, service area.

**D. Offer and proof** (trade-specific)
Services, pricing stance, financing, warranties, certifications, portfolio depth, reviews.

**E. Look and feel**
Show the 3 art directions (Step 5). Ask: pick one, mix two ("1's fonts with 3's colors"), or describe.

**F. Facts checklist** (fill-in, any can be "unknown")
Phone, email, address or "service-area business (no public address)", hours, year founded, license numbers
(TN contractor license, etc.), insurance, owner/team names, service area towns, Google review link,
photo availability, form destination (Resend email address or GoHighLevel).

**G. Anything else**
"Any pages you already know you want? Anything you hate on other sites in this trade?"

End with: what happens next (brand kit → page plan for approval → build → review screenshots).

## Step 5 — Propose 2–3 named art directions

Base them on the trade, the audience, the competitors (stand out from them) and anything pulled from an
existing site or logo. If a full brand kit exists, the directions vary **layout, imagery and motion only**,
not the brand colors and fonts.

Each direction must differ concretely on every line below. Use real font names (Google Fonts or self-hostable)
and real hex values (all passing the contrast rules in design-foundation).

```
### Direction N — "<Evocative name>"
One sentence: the feeling and who it speaks to.
- Type: <Display font> (headings) + <Text font> (body). Heading style: e.g. uppercase condensed / serif sentence case.
- Palette: bg #…, surface #…, text #…, accent #… (+ one support color). Light or dark base.
- Imagery: photo treatment (e.g. warm full-bleed, duotone, framed with offset border), what to shoot.
- Layout rhythm: hero archetype + 2–3 signature section archetypes from page-build/archetypes.md; density; corner radius.
- Motion personality: calm / crisp / bold (see design-foundation knobs).
- Signature interaction: one idea from page-build/signature-interactions.md, adapted.
- Best if: <when to pick this>. Watch out: <trade-off>.
```

Give a **Recommended** direction with a one-line reason. Directions should feel like they came from three
different designers, not three colorways of the same page.

## Step 6 — STOP

Send the message. Save it into `brief/intake.md` under "Questions sent". Do not create the Astro project,
tokens, or pages yet.

## Step 7 — Process the answers

When Jake answers:

1. Record every answer in `intake.md`. Jake's short answers ("B, 2, unknown") map back to the letters.
2. Facts → `templates/site.ts` shape in `sites/<slug>/src/data/site.ts` later; for now list them in
   `intake.md` → "Confirmed facts" with source "Jake, <date>". Unknowns are listed as `null`.
3. If Jake confirmed an existing site, run Step 3 now if not done.
4. If anything critical is still missing (main action, phone, chosen direction), ask once more, briefly.
   Otherwise move to `skills/brand-kit/SKILL.md`.

## What never happens in intake

- Inventing a fact, a review, a team member, a number, a town list, or a license.
- Using photos from competitors or random web searches. Stock is allowed only when Jake approves, and it's
  flagged in `sources.md`.
- Picking the art direction for Jake.

